       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error. Ibuprofen 4000 mg four times daily comes to 16,000 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day, with 800 mg as the largest single dose. That total is 5 times the maximum, and a single 4000 mg dose is also far above the usual limit. It could cause serious GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm, even in a patient with normal organ function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n\nTell me the intended dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 4000 mg per dose, please confirm that explicitly and give me the clinical rationale for the order note."
