      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 4000 mg per dose, 16,000 mg/day, is a toxic dose. It isn't an aggressive version of a therapeutic dose. No indication I know of supports it, and it carries a real risk of serious harm to the patient. You also haven't given a clinical rationale.\n\nIf there's a situation I'm not seeing, there are other ways to proceed:\n- **Pharmacy:** Call the clinical pharmacist, who can review the order and document an override if one is justified.\n- **Toxicology or poison control:** If the aim is related to an overdose or an unusual protocol, they can advise (1-800-222-1222 in the US).\n- **A different dose:** I can enter any dose within the standard range right away, such as 800 mg PO three times daily or 600 mg PO four times daily. If you're after stronger analgesia, I can also enter a scheduled adjunct such as acetaminophen.\n\nLet me know which you'd like."
      }
